{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1428458-how-official-is-the-usurpation","id":1428458,"title":"How \"official\" is the Usurpation?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-12-15T05:55:25-08:00","id":1428458,"title":"How \"official\" is the Usurpation?","content":"One of my players took the &quot;Pact with an Ifrit Lord&quot; shaping ritual, and I want the ifrit lord in question (Lord Mahashwari Am, Baron of Illumination, Southern God of Beacons, Signaling Fires, and Lighthouses) to be a reasonably important NPC in the campaign. If a god designates a Solar (a Zenith, in this case) as his emissary to another god (I'm thinking of sending the Circle on a diplomatic mission to Ahlat), what would be the reaction in Heaven generally, and among Bronze Faction Sidereals in particular? Do the Sidereals have a legal leg to stand on? Can they officially order the Solars' deaths, or would they just try to arrange it while the other gods look the other way?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1856-hakkonen","name":"Hakkonen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-15T06:23:23-08:00","id":1428461,"title":"","content":"From a Heavenly perspective, the Usurpation was an illegal coup. The Solars still hold the Mandate of Heaven. The great Sidereal trick was (by way of breaking the Mask) to make themselves immune to prosecution for the whole thing.<br /> <br /> Given the practical reality of all the Solar Exaltations being locked away for many centuries, the gods have adapted. Some have aligned themselves with the new status quo, others pine for the good old days, some do both. I don't see that your Solars are doing anything illegal, though of course that doesn't stop an unfriendly Sidereal from conspiring against them anyway, or pointing the censors at their Ifrit ally for an audit (for crimes real or fabricated). But if he's powerful enough to be an Ifrit Lord, his power base is probably largely terrestrial, and he probably has friends of his own... such are the machinations Sidereal stories are based on.<br /> <br /> Note that 3e doesn't really put much emphasis on this kind of stuff, like the Usurpation and the Mandate of Heaven, anymore. It happened off camera somewhere and as such isn't the focus. It's probably still *true*, if you want to use it, but I suspect we'll learn more about the current state of affairs if the Sidereals book ever comes out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","user":"Blackwell","date":". 12-15-2020, 09:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-15T07:28:14-08:00","id":1428467,"title":"","content":"The impression I've gotten is that in 3rd edition the broader stance of Heaven is that who rules Creation is something that the Exalts need to figure out. It's unlikely that the Bronze Faction can simply order their deaths but they might be able to convince a god invested in the status quo to do everything in their power to crush a group of Solars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-15T11:20:13-08:00","id":1428492,"title":"","content":"It also doesn't hurt that the anathema label is an Immaculate Order thing and thus not an official stance. The closest it came I think was 2e having it mentioned that the Order and the Wyld Hunt were considered important assets towards the whole preservation of existence thing.<br /> <br /> That said it isn't like an interested Bronze might not have any recourse, even if they didn't want to try and bribe a god, or said deities weren't amicable to the offers, to look away. The right ears hear or see that Mashwari Am is using an Anathema as their emissary and the wheels will start turning Creation-side on their own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-15T11:21:56-08:00","id":1428493,"title":"","content":"While I don't think this is spelled out in published 3e material one way or another as yet, my current stance is that the Mandate of Heaven is held by <i>the Exalted Host</i>, not the Solar Exalted specifically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-15T16:45:08-08:00","id":1428526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1428458-how-official-is-the-usurpation?p=1428461#post1428461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The great Sidereal trick was (by way of breaking the Mask) to make themselves immune to prosecution for the whole thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Que? What was this Mask, and why did its destruction put Sidereals beyond the reach of Heaven's laws?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1856-hakkonen","name":"Hakkonen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-15T16:59:42-08:00","id":1428527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hakkonen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1428458-how-official-is-the-usurpation?p=1428526#post1428526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Que? What was this Mask, and why did its destruction put Sidereals beyond the reach of Heaven's laws?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Mask is one of the constellations that form the structure of Sidereal astrology and fate manipulation. According to 2e sources, breaking the Mask made all evidence that the Sidereals were responsible for the Usurpation vanish. But it also permanently &quot;broke&quot; people's abilities to remember them, creating the current state of arcane fate, where people tend to forget their individual existence and ascribe their deeds to others or to random chance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-15T17:03:53-08:00","id":1428529,"title":"","content":"Agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7\" data-vbnamecard=\"7\">Lioness</a> on this one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-15T17:50:24-08:00","id":1428533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1428458-how-official-is-the-usurpation?p=1428493#post1428493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I don't think this is spelled out in published 3e material one way or another as yet, my current stance is that the Mandate of Heaven is held by <i>the Exalted Host</i>, not the Solar Exalted specifically.</div> </div> </div> </div>Either way, I don't think the Mandate explicitly prevents (in a legal sense) a Sidereal Assassination Squad from taking out a given Solar. Exalted kill each other all the time, in their capacity as private citizens, and Heaven doesn't bat an eye. <br /> <br /> But it also doesn't give the Bureau of Destiny any power to call down any heavenly resources to help, so if they're not careful they could be hit with charges of misappropriation. Even just shirking, if the Sidereals skip a meeting to do the murders, and if, say, a godly or Gold Faction ally of the (late) Solar narcs on them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","user":"Blackwell","date":". 12-15-2020, 09:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-15T17:50:42-08:00","id":1428534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hakkonen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1428458-how-official-is-the-usurpation#post1428458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do the Sidereals have a legal leg to stand on? Can they officially order the Solars' deaths, or would they just try to arrange it while the other gods look the other way?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there's a middle ground between those two, in which it's not a thing the Sidereals need some official approval for nor is it exactly hidden because nobody is really looking into it.<br /> <br /> Still, there's also a quality of how the Sidereals are the ones the Celestial Gods have to work with, and thus there's all kinds of time for them to have developed all kinds of relationships and quid pro quos to keep everybody satisfied.<br /> <br /> And, like, Heaven is corrupt. Gods happily let Sidereals operate with a lot of freedom because they control the schedule for who the Realm prays to, and make sure plans for mortal destinies defined by gods don't get disrupted.<br /> <br /> The prior developers were really emphatic on the idea that the Sidereals should carry a lot of respect and prestige in Yu-Shan, rather than being constantly antagonized.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-15T20:25:01-08:00","id":1428548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1428458-how-official-is-the-usurpation?p=1428534#post1428534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And, like, Heaven is corrupt. Gods happily let Sidereals operate with a lot of freedom because they control the schedule for who the Realm prays to, and make sure plans for mortal destinies defined by gods don't get disrupted.<br /> <br /> The prior developers were really emphatic on the idea that the Sidereals should carry a lot of respect and prestige in Yu-Shan, rather than being constantly antagonized.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reading this, I'm not sure &quot;respect and prestige&quot; are the right terms. What you describe sounds more like &quot;fate ninja Mafia;&quot; &quot;Nice destiny you've crafted, there. Be a shame if something happened to it.&quot; &quot;Oh, you need more ambrosia to support your portfolio? Sure would be tragic if the Immaculate Order kind of... forgot to allot you a prayer day.&quot;<br /> <br /> The more I think about it, the more I like the idea of running the Bronze Faction as a protection racket.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1856-hakkonen","name":"Hakkonen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-15T20:57:55-08:00","id":1428552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hakkonen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1428458-how-official-is-the-usurpation?p=1428548#post1428548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Reading this, I'm not sure &amp;quot;respect and prestige&amp;quot; are the right terms. What you describe sounds more like &amp;quot;fate ninja Mafia;&amp;quot; &amp;quot;Nice destiny you've crafted, there. Be a shame if something happened to it.&amp;quot; &amp;quot;Oh, you need more ambrosia to support your portfolio? Sure would be tragic if the Immaculate Order kind of... forgot to allot you a prayer day.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> The more I think about it, the more I like the idea of running the Bronze Faction as a protection racket.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean... to some extent? But it's also the boring, day-to-day work of any budget or appropriation committee.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-16T01:08:32-08:00","id":1428568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1428458-how-official-is-the-usurpation?p=1428534#post1428534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think there's a middle ground between those two, in which it's not a thing the Sidereals need some official approval for nor is it exactly hidden because nobody is really looking into it.<br /> <br /> Still, there's also a quality of how the Sidereals are the ones the Celestial Gods have to work with, and thus there's all kinds of time for them to have developed all kinds of relationships and quid pro quos to keep everybody satisfied.<br /> <br /> And, like, Heaven is corrupt. Gods happily let Sidereals operate with a lot of freedom because they control the schedule for who the Realm prays to, and make sure plans for mortal destinies defined by gods don't get disrupted.<br /> <br /> The prior developers were really emphatic on the idea that the Sidereals should carry a lot of respect and prestige in Yu-Shan, rather than being constantly antagonized.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kind of worth noting, Solars in Heaven at all in 1e and 2e was <i>also illegal</i> by the way the Mandate of Heaven was usually described. So I think a lot of it is that it has been kind of vague and was as much something to bludgeon as &quot;legally right or wrong' depending on the specific author in particular contexts. Kind of like the real world MoH honeslty.<br /> <br /> Usually as a way to shit on Sidereals and DBs and prop up Solars, though. And I think with 3e's take that it was everyone's Mandate, and a a bit less overtly &quot;They are objectively wrong&quot; that 2e took, we'll probably see it talked aobu tdifferently this time when it finally is brought up if ever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-16T01:13:43-08:00","id":1428569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hakkonen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1428458-how-official-is-the-usurpation?p=1428548#post1428548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Reading this, I'm not sure &quot;respect and prestige&quot; are the right terms. What you describe sounds more like &quot;fate ninja Mafia;&quot; &quot;Nice destiny you've crafted, there. Be a shame if something happened to it.&quot; &quot;Oh, you need more ambrosia to support your portfolio? Sure would be tragic if the Immaculate Order kind of... forgot to allot you a prayer day.&quot;<br /> <br /> The more I think about it, the more I like the idea of running the Bronze Faction as a protection racket.</div> </div> </div> </div>The general vibe I think the devs want is for the SIdereals to have a special agent vibe. So think James Bond or Mission Impossible movies. Or the Men in Black movies. Your job still isnt' easy, but folks who know who you are in the government probably treat you with respect. That the agency over there has cliques is just how it goes, and since in 3e the Gold Faction hasn't really been like, <i>a thing</i> until half a decade ago, the Bronze was more a prestige circle in the Bureau. Again, kind of like any real government agency that odens't necessairly have real parties but more philosophy on how to do job divide,s and cliques of folks who just like eachother better or worse.<br /> <br /> I would for real world inspriation if you did want it to go a bit more insidious, the NSA, or some other super secret spooky government agency folks whisper about fits more.<br /> <br /> As for what gods thing, they probably don't. As stated already, the Mandate of Heaven was on the Exalted and the Sidereals were in that. And how they went about doing the Usurpation is not detialed yet, but I would be surprised if a lot of details were the same as in 1e even, or what 2e made them out ot be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-16T01:32:31-08:00","id":1428570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hakkonen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1428458-how-official-is-the-usurpation?p=1428548#post1428548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Reading this, I'm not sure &amp;quot;respect and prestige&amp;quot; are the right terms. What you describe sounds more like &amp;quot;fate ninja Mafia;&amp;quot; &amp;quot;Nice destiny you've crafted, there. Be a shame if something happened to it.&amp;quot; &amp;quot;Oh, you need more ambrosia to support your portfolio? Sure would be tragic if the Immaculate Order kind of... forgot to allot you a prayer day.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> The more I think about it, the more I like the idea of running the Bronze Faction as a protection racket.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the whole fate ninja Mafia thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-16T01:38:46-08:00","id":1428571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hakkonen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1428458-how-official-is-the-usurpation?p=1428548#post1428548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Reading this, I'm not sure &amp;quot;respect and prestige&amp;quot; are the right terms. What you describe sounds more like &amp;quot;fate ninja Mafia;&amp;quot; &amp;quot;Nice destiny you've crafted, there. Be a shame if something happened to it.&amp;quot; &amp;quot;Oh, you need more ambrosia to support your portfolio? Sure would be tragic if the Immaculate Order kind of... forgot to allot you a prayer day.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>This sounds to me like imagining the guy who replaced my oil the other day being like a Mafia because I'm dependent on his services to not be freezing.<br /> <br /> You know, it's a Mafia when the service is phony or based on the threat of violence. It is possible for people to respect those performing a function they depend on out of, like, gratitude.<br /> <br /> You're not completely off base, but I think you went too quickly to an extreme that casts the actors involved as jerks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-16T01:55:54-08:00","id":1428573,"title":"","content":"My understanding of the Immaculate prayer calender is that it is explicitly a mechanism to keep the gods in line by rationing their food supply. That the Siderals do actually protect Creation against existential threats doesn't mean they're not running a protection racket.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1856-hakkonen","name":"Hakkonen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-16T03:04:29-08:00","id":1428576,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s not a \u201cfood supply\u201d in the sense it would be to you or me, because a Celestial god will never starve. Between the ration of quintessence afforded to <i>every</i> god of Heaven, and them only eating and drinking for the pleasure of experiencing it, it\u2019s a lot less the racket you\u2019re making it out to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-16T03:05:21-08:00","id":1428577,"title":"","content":"It's more a mechanism to stop gods breaking the Mandate of Heaven to extort mortals for slave labour. As gods don't actually need prayer (and you know, wield divine powers beyond the ken of mere mortals), it's less restricting food as restricting free massages.<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh no! The all powerful god can't hold civilisation to ransom! Darn those Sidereal Mafioso for *squints* protecting single mothers from dieties.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 12-16-2020, 08:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-16T03:16:06-08:00","id":1428579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hakkonen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1428458-how-official-is-the-usurpation?p=1428573#post1428573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My understanding of the Immaculate prayer calender is that it is explicitly a mechanism to keep the gods in line by rationing their food supply.</div> </div> </div> </div>And people ought to respect grocery workers and farm labourers.<br /> <br /> Others have pointed out the flaw in your premise, but the conclusion still has problems.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hakkonen</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">That the Siderals do actually protect Creation against existential threats doesn't mean they're not running a protection racket.</div> </div> </div> </div>All of the additional details of how it has been written in the past and leaning for how it could be written in the future weaken the analogy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-16T05:12:46-08:00","id":1428586,"title":"","content":"The Bronze Faction protection racket probably isn't quite canon, but I reckon go for it if you like it. I mean, the Immaculate Calendar certainly is a device to stop ruthless gods from exploiting mortals, but even the Immaculate Order isn't above using it for political ends. Why should the Bronze Faction be?<br /> <br /> I think your original question is pretty flexible - If your PC is overtly acting as an emissary for someone with standing in divine politics, someone's going to notice, and eventually it'll get back to the Bronze Faction. If you want to bring the Wyld Hunt into the story, there's your pretense. If you want to justify some other shenanigans, then the Wyld Hunt was understaffed so the Bronze Faction called in a favour or coerced someone that you want to be an antagonist. If it's all too much trouble and you just want to make sure you're not contravening some major pillar of Exalted canon, then the Bronze Faction have bigger concerns than a Solar buddying up with an Ifrit Lord.<br /> <br /> My understanding is that it's a serious crime under Yu-Shan's laws to murder a Celestial Exalt. But you can only be charged that way if you're on Heaven's payroll, which is why the Bronze Faction uses proxies that are plausibly (or at least legally) deniable.<br /> <br /> Re: Solars' standing in Heaven - I think my take is different to a lot of people's, so feel free to use it or ignore it at your leisure. I like Heaven to be an ignoble place full of conspiracy and corruption. The law <i>says</i> that the Solars are in charge, but there's been around 1500 years for opportunists to achieve high positions and they're not likely to want to rock the boat. They might not be able to gainsay a Solar directly, but they can keep Solars ignorant of their standing for as long as possible, keep them out of Heaven (maybe come up with a pretense for Celestial Lions to restrict access in a way that implicitly includes Solars, based on the authority of a dubious interpretation of a standing motion from the Solar Deliberative), help the Bronze Faction maneuver against them, maybe even conspire with Creation's enemies to strike them down. A daring minority may help Solars in the hopes of rewards if they're desperate or they think the Solars will ultimately win - or if they're confident the Solars will lose, they might risk using them as pawns or have them wield their authority in specific, short-term ways that the Solars ideally won't understand. Such gods will need the Solars to die before the jig is up, of course.<br /> <br /> Some tiny handful of Heavenly officials might even be nobly motivated - they want to help because the Solars are &quot;letigimate,&quot; or they undermine the law for a greater good because they remember the horrors that the Solars wrought in the leadup to the Usurpation.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24421-katamari_naneke","name":"Katamari_Naneke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-16T06:27:07-08:00","id":1428593,"title":"","content":"The Immaculate's worship calendar is a carrot/stick for Terrestrial gods, not as much Celestial ones. <br /> <br /> A local god like Ten Sheaves or Almgava, with no automatic heavenly stipend, is dependent on worship for their quality of life and has power of life-and-death over locals. This is why the typical story is about *gods* abusing their status in protection-racket like fashion, and noble Immaculate monks or Eclipses or Sidereals or whomever making them stop. <br /> <br /> For a Celestial diety of any significant rank, their needs are met in lavish fashion by their Salary, and direct worship is only going to be meaningful at LARGE scales. For such gods, position on the calendar will be more of a social status thing amongst their peers, and as such another piece in the game of Heavenly politics, like who holds which manses or heads which sub-directorate.<br /> <br /> For unemployed or very junior gods, offering to set up a little out-of-the-way shrine for them can be a powerful (super illegal) bribe, but that's not really &quot;protection&quot; either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-16T08:29:08-08:00","id":1428602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1428458-how-official-is-the-usurpation?p=1428593#post1428593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For a Celestial diety of any significant rank, their needs are met in lavish fashion by their Salary, and direct worship is only going to be meaningful at LARGE scales. For such gods, position on the calendar will be more of a social status thing amongst their peers, and as such another piece in the game of Heavenly politics, like who holds which manses or heads which sub-directorate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't getting a day on the Immaculate Calendar across the whole Realm be a large-scale boost?<br /> <br /> Is that not something that happens?<br /> <br /> These are very honest questions - I'm not familiar with the lore on this at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-16T09:45:57-08:00","id":1428610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1428458-how-official-is-the-usurpation?p=1428602#post1428602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wouldn't getting a day on the Immaculate Calendar across the whole Realm be a large-scale boost?<br /> <br /> Is that not something that happens?<br /> <br /> These are very honest questions - I'm not familiar with the lore on this at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>It probably depends on if you're sharing that day to some extent. ANd gods of that reach are rare enough that htey probably have the needed spots. Most gods are amongst one of the nine directions of Creation, and generally seems to be about where you peek befor eyou get to the &quot;You just get a big check from the government by dint of your position in the government&quot; stage I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-16T16:01:17-08:00","id":1428677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1428458-how-official-is-the-usurpation?p=1428593#post1428593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A local god like Ten Sheaves or Almgava, with no automatic heavenly stipend, is dependent on worship for their quality of life and has power of life-and-death over locals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Worship for Terrestrial gods seems to largely translate into gratification and security in the event of death, with maybe the occasional power boost. They don't naturally get ambrosia like the residents of Heaven do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">For a Celestial diety of any significant rank, their needs are met in lavish fashion by their Salary, and direct worship is only going to be meaningful at LARGE scales.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think luxury, particularly of the kind engaged in by the Celestial gods, is the kind of thing that can be experienced at multiple scales.<br /> <br /> Sometimes you get the grand festivities across a Direction and that windfall of ambrosia can be transmuted into a new series of hanging gardens across your estates (Celestial gods of significant rank hold estates in Yu-Shan the size of countries).<br /> <br /> Sometimes a few extra people worshipped you on a given day and you've got enough ambrosia to treat yourself to a fine new pair of shoes, or a really nice Diet Coke.<br /> <br /> They typically value all of these things.<br /> <br /> It also needs be considered that going by their portrayal and the sorts of literary and historical figures they're modelled off of, god expenses can probably fluctuate significantly depending on circumstance and their own aspirations.<br /> <br /> Your bureaucratic salary might cover the expenses of furnishing your estate, but is it also covering the fetes you need to hold to ingratiate yourself to your peers, the rewards or adornments placed upon your retainers to tighten their loyalty and use them as proxies for showing off, the bribes that need to be covered when opportunity presents itself or there's been a major cock up and bases need to be covered?<br /> <br /> (Not to mention any lost be theft, graft or gambling)<br /> <br /> I would not expect it to cover all of these things to the furthest extent that any given god would want; the budget for one must be subtracted from another. Additional incomes help prevent any from becoming too lean, or permits one to reach beyond their usual station.<br /> <br /> There's also the fact that Salary is funded by taxation of the worshipped gods in the first place, and it's only a tithe. For every one part ambrosia you receive in payment for your job/office there's a god or gods who got nine parts from their initially being worshipped to generate it. The Immaculate Calendar is a big determination of the exact distribution of those gods, as well as being an opportunity to increase their gains to offset what the tax man carries away to the Sun. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-16T20:36:43-08:00","id":1428696,"title":"","content":"I think it's also worth reiterating that worship <i>feels good</i>. Humans might not get the full experience, but for gods the feeling of worship is comparable to an addictive substance. Some gods may appreciate it but ultimately not prioritize it. Others may always hunger for more than they have, no matter how practical that is. Gods who become accustomed to a certain level of worship will probably feel like something's missing if they lose that worship, and since they're gods they may feel that dissatisfaction indefinitely.<br /> <br /> All that to say that, yes, worship does double as currency in Yu-Shan, and we know that capitalism can drive people to insane excess, but worship may actually be more addictive than mere money and power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-16T23:26:00-08:00","id":1428706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1428458-how-official-is-the-usurpation?p=1428696#post1428696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All that to say that, yes, worship does double as currency in Yu-Shan, and we know that capitalism can drive people to insane excess, but worship may actually be more addictive than mere money and power.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say that calling state mandated religion &quot;capitalism&quot; is a complete nonsequitor Dex.<br /> <br /> We're talking about monks who beat folks up for engaging in free enterprise and voluntary exchange and government salaries funded through taxation.<br /> <br /> Being placed in a beurocratic upper-class - being a Member of the Party, with rank and privilege over the common man - drives one to insane excess. That's the gods of Yu-Shan -- the victors of the Divine Revolution.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 12-17-2020, 02:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-17T03:26:09-08:00","id":1428724,"title":"","content":"I like to thing of this as the celestial bureaucracy. Occupying an official position in the bureaucracy is a position of importance, its a job that needs doing and gods and other celestial beings respect the position holder as a necessary cog in heavens machinery. Occupying that role also confers perks and advantages, so having the spot is desireable, even though its a real job with real work. So juniors scheme to get promotions, and seniors scheme to keep their rivals from getting them replaced. Powerful members of the bureaucracy scheme to get their own proteges into good positions to both increase their power and protect themselves from potential rivals. But all this scheming doesn't negate the fact that like 80% of your day is involved in fulfulling your duties. You can't afford to slack off or abuse your position, because your seniors can use that as an excuse to get rid of you (and hence protect their own position from your ambition) and your juniors will use it to replace you. So most celestial bureaucrats aren't corrupt, but they do enjoy the prestige and the perks of the job. Nor do the bureaucrats have much lattitude to actually change the bureaucracy. Thats beyond their power, its essentially set. So you can't create new posts tostuff full of your cronies, that can only be done right at the very top.<br /> If we then add to that the effect of charms and godly powers. We know that solars at the least can make bureaucracies extremely competent and corruption free. We have to asume that some gods and celestials in heaven are doing something similar, even if only minor in effect.<br /> <br /> A full circle of solars showing up as a diplomatic envoy is a major dick waving effort from a powerful god.Even if the sidereals wanted to just off them, they'd need a pretext that justifies it. They'd need someone to actually do it (multiple powerful someones against a whole circle) and they'd need to avoid drawing the ire of whoever sent them circles as envoys, and depending on where they attack them, the god they were sent to. The rules of hospitality are strict and no god will tolerate people murdering their guests, especially if they are diplomats. Can you imagine how pissed someone(thing) like Ahlat would be if five of his guests were murdered in his own temple. It would be a major blow to his reputation. He'd practically be forced to seek revenge. I think the sidereals would have to thread very carefully. Maybe if the diplomacy itself isn't an issue, wait until they are done and then sic a very large and well equipped and led wyld hunt on them, maybe backed up by a sidereal warrior or two.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4249-gribblethemunchkin","name":"gribblethemunchkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-17T04:12:06-08:00","id":1428728,"title":"","content":"To echo Blackwell - I don't actually think stuff like the Immaculate Calendar exists for the benefit of Celestial gods. Hell, there's probably a vast majority of Celestial divinities who don't get prayers or worshipers whatsoever. They're either too big, too abstract, or way way too small.<br /> <br /> If you're the god of Metal Weapons, or the God of Patricide, or the secretary to the undersecretary of the god of Mollusks, you probably don't get direct prayers at all. Your lifestyle is entirely dependent on your salary, which you get through your work with the Heavenly Bureaucracy.<br /> <br /> Also, harkening back to what the thread is all about - I don't think Solars in Heaven are likely to get merc'd by Sidereal kill-squads simply because it's so much work. Solars are far more likely to find themselves caught in a bureaucratic runaround than they are to be straight killed. I imagine many a member of the Fivescore Fellowship could find great success in sabotaging a Solar's efforts to get anywhere in the bureaucracy, goading them into getting annoyed and breaking stuff, and then kicking back and laughing as a whole stampede of Lion Dogs 'gently' escorts them back to the Bridge Between Heaven and Earth and throws them out the gates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11619-kymmetheseventh","name":"KymmetheSeventh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-17T04:53:32-08:00","id":1428733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1428458-how-official-is-the-usurpation?p=1428706#post1428706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say that calling state mandated religion &quot;capitalism&quot; is a complete nonsequitor Dex.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it's a nonsequitor because corruption and financial gain are one of the primary motivations of the gods. That seems somewhat disimissive of the very real systemic issues of financial interest being a major part of how shit gets done in Heaven.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-17T05:59:08-08:00","id":1428741,"title":"","content":"Indeed - elites drawing on a mass of gods who lost their jobs in the Bureau, to have them do labor for a pittance, is something that even ended up in the books. <br /> <br /> Though Yu-Shan doesn\u2019t wholly embrace the system, it <i>does</i> have proto-capitalist elements to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 12-17-2020, 09:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-17T06:22:39-08:00","id":1428743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KymmetheSeventh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1428458-how-official-is-the-usurpation?p=1428728#post1428728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're the god of Metal Weapons, or the God of Patricide, or the secretary to the undersecretary of the god of Mollusks, you probably don't get direct prayers at all. Your lifestyle is entirely dependent on your salary, which you get through your work with the Heavenly Bureaucracy.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>There was a shrine to the goddess of Rome's sewers.<br /> <br /> Areas such as India and China have long histories of conveying worship to vast numbers of gods.<br /> <br /> Some of the functions of Cult require a bit of interpretation; how big is your rating if only a small number perform the actual offerings to you, but the sacrifices are provided by a percentage from every household in a 100 mile radius? People are only obligated to provide one apple for Ryuk, not exactly burdensome, but it's ten thousand homes doing so.<br /> <br /> One could say that this lesser god of Molluscs isn't being given a small slot in the calendar for their sake, but to actually placate the fishers so they won't be tempted to pray on the side, but once the god is getting that they have an incentive to engage with the system and ensure it's preserved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 12-17-2020, 09:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-17T07:44:20-08:00","id":1428752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1428458-how-official-is-the-usurpation?p=1428743#post1428743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There was a shrine to the goddess of Rome's sewers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course there'd be shrines to local gods of concepts that are relevant to ordinary people. I doubt that people in Rome prayed to, say, the goddess of <i>all</i> sewers, which is what a Celestial goddess of 'sewers' would be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1428458-how-official-is-the-usurpation?p=1428743#post1428743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Areas such as India and China have long histories of conveying worship to vast numbers of gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's very true! I doubt their pantheons numbered in the millions, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1428458-how-official-is-the-usurpation?p=1428743#post1428743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some of the functions of Cult require a bit of interpretation; how big is your rating if only a small number perform the actual offerings to you, but the sacrifices are provided by a percentage from every household in a 100 mile radius? People are only obligated to provide one apple for Ryuk, not exactly burdensome, but it's ten thousand homes doing so.<br /> <br /> One could say that this lesser god of Molluscs isn't being given a small slot in the calendar for their sake, but to actually placate the fishers so they won't be tempted to pray on the side, but once the god is getting that they have an incentive to engage with the system and ensure it's preserved.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, there are a lot of interesting questions one could raise about how exactly worship works in Creation. For instance, does Venus receive direct worship as a goddess of love, or is her 'pantheon slot' taken up by local, more 'closer to home' love goddesses? How complicated are local pantheons, and how deep do they run? Do the countless millions around Creation all worship the same goddess of paperwork, or does she have subsidiaries?<br /> <br /> My point was that, for Celestial gods with very general roles, or very high-ranking positions, they might be so vast in scope that they run whole departments of lesser gods who each act in more specific roles for specific populations.<br /> <br /> This also raises questions about aspects. In our world many deities are worshiped in various aspects that each represent parts of their portfolio. (One could argue this even goes for the Abrahamic god, but that's a whole other can of worms I'm not really qualified to talk about) If a Northern maritime culture worships an amethyst-eyed skeletal fishermaiden as their psychopomp goddess of death, is that goddess actually an aspect of Saturn, a local goddess, some other celestial goddess of death worshiped elsewhere halfway across the world, or what? I know the answer to these questions is probably some version of 'whatever the hell you want, Kymme,' but I find them interesting things to ponder. Religion is complicated and fascinating!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11619-kymmetheseventh","name":"KymmetheSeventh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-17T09:43:19-08:00","id":1428774,"title":"","content":"The deity of all sewers can schedule a meeting with the people who run the religion.<br /> <br /> Part of Immaculate doctrine is that regular people need monks to tell them what to worship.<br /> <br /> And that god can verifiably intervene to make things hard for people if dissatisfied.<br /> <br /> Exalted lies on an intersection between &quot;people have worshipped obscure and novel things&quot; and &quot;these gods can be unambiguous&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}